# nflverse feeds are large and reproducible from their release assets. The
# schedule is committed because the credit arithmetic must be re-checkable,
# and the probe cache because it is bought evidence.
data/raw/nfl/pbp/
data/raw/nfl/player_stats/
data/raw/nfl/weekly_rosters/
data/raw/nfl/depth_charts/
data/raw/nfl/snap_counts/
data/raw/nfl/rosters/
data/raw/nfl/injuries/
data/processed/*.csv
data/raw/nfl/historical_prices/

# Single-season backtest bets. `run_props_backtest.py` writes one of these per
# season; the pooled `*_props_backtest_bets.csv` that four reports read comes
# only from `run_props_replication.py`. They shared a filename until
# 2026-08-31, and a partial set of season files committed alongside the pooled
# one is the same confusion in a different shape.
data/outputs/*_props_backtest_bets_[0-9]*.csv
